title: Coup in Heartland
subtitle: The Chancellor attempts to overthrow the Heartland government.
view-if: chancellor == "Goodryke" and altona_seen and marcher_heartland and not presidential_powers and not heartland_reichsexekution
on-arrival: heartland_coup_seen = 1; otl_heartland_coup_seen = 1; strife += 2; staal_marcher_r -= 1; staal_marcher_support -= 1
new-page: true
tags: event
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/Commonwealth Army.jpg

= Coup in Heartland

A crisis! Chancellor [+ chancellor +] has ordered the dismissal of the Heartland government through a procedure known as the <i>Commonwealth intervention</i>. He claims the state government can no longer maintain order amid escalating street battles between the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span>, the Banners, and other paramilitary groups—despite his own administration having legalized them.

[? if not altona_good: The recent clashes in Abysm have handed him the pretext to depose the Heartland government?][? if altona_good: The surge in politically motivated violence has given Goodryke the pretext to depose the Heartland government?]. [? if heartland_leader == "Bristol": With Lyle Bristol still abroad on convalescent leave following the heartbreaking events of the past few months?][? if heartland_leader != "Bristol": With Minister-President [+ heartland_leader +] unwilling to risk a civil war to defend his administration?], Goodryke is moving to seize control. If this coup is successful, Goodryke will transfer control of Heartland to a <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i>, a calculated move to win over the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> by granting the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> free rein in the state. We suspect Defense Minister Staal to be the mastermind behind this scheme—another step in advancing his <span class="tooltip-text" title="Coined by conservative elites like Staal and Goodryke, this strategy aims to control the dynamic Royalist movement and integrate it into the state by introducing the party to government. In their eyes, this would moderate the Royalists, transforming them into a constructive component of the state.">taming strategy</span>.

The legality of this action is dubious. Heath has responded that he'll only yield to force. Many of our members are prepared to resist.

- @defend
- @surrender

@defend
title: Fight against the overthrow attempt!
subtitle: Labor will call a general strike. The the Banners and the loyal elements of the Heartland police will resist the coup.
unavailable-subtitle: We do not have the forces to resist.
choose-if: democracy_force >= 35

[? if heartland_leader == "Sedgewick" or heartland_leader == "Askew": A potential roadblock to armed resistance is the unwillingness of Minister President [+ heartland_leader +] to do so, [? if not banner_stay:as a result, they've overruled Heath's call to resist the coup and has made the whole situation a mess. ?][? if banner_stay:however, the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>'s decision to remain in a militarized the Banners has rallied the Unity Coalition parties to the defense of the republic they helped create. ?] ?]

The Commonwealth Army are already on the streets of Axton, with a national force of a hundred thousand men on standby, ready to crush any resistance. The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> and the recently legalized <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> are poised to back them. The the Banners simply cannot match the small, but well-trained and heavily armed Commonwealth Army. If we resist, we face the very real prospect of civil war. We understand the gravity of this, don’t we?

- @defend_2: We will fight, even if it leads to a civil war.
- @defend_3: We will fight, even if it leads to a civil war.
- @surrender

@defend_2
view-if: (royalist_votes >= 25 or banner_militancy < 0.2) and ((army_strength*army_militancy*(1-army_loyalty)) >= banner_strength*banner_militancy) and (marcher_votes < 26 or banner_militancy < 0.2) and banner_militancy < 0.3
on-arrival: {!

Q.loyalist_force_heartland = Q.loyalist_strength*Q.loyalist_militancy;
Q.warden_force_heartland = Q.warden_strength*Q.warden_militancy;
Q.banner_force_heartland = Q.banner_strength*Q.banner_militancy;
Q.vanguard_force_heartland = Q.vanguard_strength*Q.vanguard_militancy;
Q.heartland_force_heartland = Q.heartland_police_strength*Q.heartland_police_militancy*Q.heartland_police_loyalty;
Q.army_force_heartland = Q.army_strength*Q.army_militancy*(1-Q.army_loyalty);
var total_force_prussia = (Q.loyalist_force_heartland+Q.warden_force_heartland+Q.banner_force_heartland+Q.vanguard_force_heartland+Q.heartland_force_heartland+Q.army_force_heartland);

Q.loyalist_force_heartland = Math.round((Q.loyalist_force_heartland/total_force_prussia)*100);
Q.warden_force_heartland = Math.round((Q.warden_force_heartland/total_force_prussia)*100);
Q.banner_force_heartland = Math.round((Q.banner_force_heartland/total_force_prussia)*100);
Q.vanguard_force_heartland = Math.round((Q.vanguard_force_heartland/total_force_prussia)*100);
Q.heartland_force_heartland = Math.round((Q.heartland_force_heartland/total_force_prussia)*100);

Q.happy_forces = Q.banner_force*(1-Q.dissent) + Q.heartland_force;
if (Q.heartland_leader == "Askew" || Q.heartland_leader == "Sedgewick" && !Q.banner_stay) Q.happy_forces -= (Q.heartland_force / 2);
if (Q.collectivist_truce) Q.happy_forces += Q.vanguard_force;
Q.happy_forces += (Q.commons_marcher_normalized*(1 - Q.dissent)*(1 - Q.disfavored/100))/5;
Q.angry_forces = Q.warden_force + Q.loyalist_force + (Q.army_force_heartland/2);

Q.resist_coup = 1
!}
go-to: calculations


@calculations
go-to: defend_2_civil_war if happy_forces < angry_forces; defend_2_victory if happy_forces >= angry_forces


@defend_2_victory
on-arrival: heartland_coup_win = 1; loyalist_strength *= 0.75; warden_strength *= 0.75; pro_republic += 12; commons_collectivist -= 4; disfavored_collectivist -= 4; commons_marcher += 8; disfavored_marcher += 8; commons_royalist -= 6; disfavored_royalist -= 6; burgher_royalist -= 4; burgher_marcher += 4; guild_royalist -= 3; guild_ddp += 2; guild_gold += 1; guild_lvp += 3; landed_royalist -= 3; landed_ddp += 2; landed_gold += 1; landed_lvp += 3; faithful_royalist -= 3; faithful_marcher += 3; coup_victory = 1; ddp_cohesion += 3; ddp_left += 3; ddp_relation += 5; lvp_left += 2; lvp_relation += 5; unionist_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 5 if banner_stay; unionist_relation += 5 if banner_stay; heartland_police_loyalty = 1; heartland_police_strength += 25; army_militancy -= 0.5; papen_strength -= 10; dufour_papen_r -= 10
achievement: bollwerk_der_demokratie
go-to: defend_2_victory_2

Our forces confront the government troops and their <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> auxiliaries on their way to seize government offices, and somehow, our enemies retreat without a fight! They were overwhelmed by our display of strength, and have chosen to slink away. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] withdraws the dismissal of the Heartland government, at least for now.

The show of force has reinvigorated support for the republic and for the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and has weakened the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span>. It’s anticipated that Chancellor Goodryke will either resign or be deposed by the Camarilla for his embarrassing failure, as DuFour’s confidence in him has been utterly shattered.

@defend_2_victory_2
achievement: drei_pfeile


@defend_2_civil_war

Our forces confront the government troops and their supporters on the streets of Axton, and armed fighting erupts. The <span style="color: #808080;">reactionaries</span> do not budge from their positions. We are caught at a disadvantage.

- @civil_war: It is a civil war.

@defend_3
view-if: not ((royalist_votes >= 25 or banner_militancy < 0.2) and ((army_strength*army_militancy*(1-army_loyalty)) >= banner_strength*banner_militancy) and (marcher_votes < 26 or banner_militancy < 0.2) and banner_militancy < 0.3)
on-arrival: papen_strength -= 1; dufour_papen_r -= 1; pro_republic += 5
achievement: bollwerk_der_demokratie

Goodryke has backed down without a fight! With Heath and the Heartland government standing firm, declaring they would only respond to force, Goodryke has refused to press ahead with his plan, unwilling to risk civil war. DuFour is reportedly displeased with Goodryke's weakness but believes another opportunity will come soon.

For now, we remain in control of the democratic bulwark.

@surrender
title: Give up on the Heartland government.
subtitle: We will attempt to fight this out legally.
on-arrival: older_heartland_leader = heartland_leader; heartland_coup_lose = 1; pre_in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 1 if ((in_weimar_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland == 1) or (in_grand_coalition_heartland == 1 and lvp_formed)); pre_in_grand_coalition_heartland = 1 if (in_grand_coalition_heartland == 1 or in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland == 1); in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; heartland_leader = "Goodryke"; commons_marcher -= 5; burgher_marcher -= 5; burgher_ddp -= 3; disfavored_marcher -= 3; left_dissent += 10; labor_dissent += 10; knight_dissent += 20; banner_militancy *= 0.8; banner_strength -= 200; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.5; next_election_time_heartland = time + 48; next_election_year_heartland = year + 4; papen_strength += 1

On the morning of the coup, the decree is presented to the Heartland government. Despite fierce objections to its constitutionality—and Heath’s vow to yield only to force—a hundred thousand Commonwealth Army troops occupy key government buildings in Axton. One by one, Heath and the police chiefs allow themselves to be removed without resistance.

A pall of hopelessness and despair descends over <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformism</span>. We have failed. Many in the the Banners simply quit, demoralized by their leaders' lack of a call to action. 

President DuFour appoints the <span style="color: #808080;">reactionary</span> Franz von Goodryke as <i>Commonwealth Commissioner</i> of Heartland, tasked with dismantling the democratic structures we fought to preserve. This furthers Goodryke’s ambition for a “New State”—one that unites the chancellorship and the Heartland premiership under a single authoritarian hand.
